  m_Name: EndingScenes_en
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Unity.Localization::UnityEngine.Localization.Tables.StringTable
  m_LocaleId:
    m_Code: en
  m_SharedData: {fileID: 11400000, guid: e8f9a0b1c2d3e4f5a6b7c8d9e0f1a2b3, type: 2}
  m_Metadata:
    m_Items: []
  m_TableData:
  - m_Id: 100000000001
    m_Localized: main menu
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000002
    m_Localized: "The cards did not lie \u2013 the revelation proved true. The evidence
      against Sir Blackmore was so overwhelming\nthat even money could not save him
      from arrest.\n\nThe motive was despicable: often performing at the badger's
      manor,\nthe fox accidentally discovered secret tunnels where he ran an underground
      fur trade.\n\nWithout telling anyone, the Fox tried to blackmail Blackmore.\nIn
      response, Sir Blackmore invited her to perform at an evening event to \xABdiscuss
      the details\xBB. And killed her.\n\nThe verdict for all these villanies was
      hailed as a \xABtriumph of justice\xBB \u2013 the badger awaited the death
      penalty by hanging.\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000003
    m_Localized: "The cards pointed to Doctor Murli \u2014 and you, of course, informed
      him of this.\n\nHis reaction was explosive: he overturned the table, smashed
      the crystal ball and several rare crystals.\n\nOnly later did you realize the
      cards were wrong. But by then the doctor's rage had already turned into conviction.\n\nHe
      dedicated his life to convincing his contemporaries that fortune-telling is
      a dangerous and utterly senseless delusion \u2014 which drove away many of
      your clients."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000004
    m_Localized: "The cards pointed to Theodore Lapwood \u2013 alas, incorrectly.
      But this was discovered too late.\n\nThe scant and circumstantial evidence
      was enough to send the poor poet to prison for a decade.\n\nIn prison his talent
      blossomed and, upon release, Lapwood published a collection of poems dedicated
      to Lisitsia \u2013 so sincere and sorrowful that it immediately made Theodore
      a celebrated poet.\n\nThe rest of Theodore's life was spent famous and wealthy
      \u2013 as if fate had decided to make a public apology."
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  - m_Id: 100000000005
    m_Localized: "The cards pointed to Lady Nottingham \u2013 and, alas, were wrong.\n\nNo
      evidence of her guilt was found, and the family's wealth allowed them to quickly
      silence the police and the press, then ruin Doctor Murli with counter-suits.\n\nHaving
      lost his reputation, Murli was forced to leave Lapdon and became a country
      doctor in a distant, forgotten village.\n\nLady Bella, finally disillusioned
      with men, invested the money raised from the scandal into opening Lapdon's
      first school for girls \u2014 and thereby gained a new fame, far more favorable.\n"
    m_Metadata:
      m_Items: []
  references:
    version: 2
    RefIds: []
